{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795515677,"nonce":"SDGzJIOg5DdDOJahRiJSGtbWW1Q=","title":"coupling: the structural probes read trainable parameters at their stored value (0 before jno.core initialises them)","message":"Found in Part B5. Coupled.__init__ probes the interface stiffness (Dirichlet side, alpha=auto, the floating-subdomain Robin) by solving each participant at its parameters stored values. A jno.np.parameter with .initialize(...) holds 0 until a jno.core setup applies the initializer, so a trainable conductivity probes a singular problem (-0 * Laplacian). The B5 test sets the stored value (eqx.tree_at). Options: apply the parameter initializer for the probe when the stored value is the placeholder, or probe at _perturbed_params as jno.dd and fdm _prepare_steady_slots do (the ratio of stiffnesses then is not the trained one).","files":null}]}